The **area function** $A(x) = \int_{a}^{x} f(t)\,dt$ measures signed area from the fixed left end $a$ to the moving right end $x$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-0.4,0) -- (6.4,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.5) -- (0,4.8) node[above] {$y$};
\fill[gray!35, domain=1.2:4, variable=\x] (1.2,0) -- plot ({\x},{1 + 0.12*(\x-0.6)*(\x-0.6)}) -- (4,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick, <->, domain=0.2:5.8, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1 + 0.12*(\x-0.6)*(\x-0.6)});
\draw[dashed] (1.2,0) -- (1.2,1.04);
\draw[dashed] (4,0) -- (4,2.39);
\node[below] at (1.2,0) {$a$};
\node[below] at (4,0) {$x$};
\node at (2.6,0.7) {$A(x)$};
\node at (3.6,4.1) {$y=f(t)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

